DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ttiimmeessppeecc__ggeett function sets the interval pointed to by _t_s to hold the
     current calendar time based on the specified time base in _b_a_s_e.

     The base TIME_UTC returns the time since the epoch.  This time is ex‐
     pressed in seconds and nanoseconds since midnight (0 hour), January 1,
     1970.  In FreeBSD, this corresponds to CLOCK_REALTIME.

     The base TIME_MONOTONIC returns a monotonically-increasing time since an
     unspecified point in the past.  In FreeBSD, this corresponds to
     CLOCK_MONOTONIC.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The ttiimmeessppeecc__ggeett function returns the passed value of _b_a_s_e if successful,
     otherwise 0 on failure.

